 ],
 "literal": "Desire greatly he has, bestowing grace also he will bestow / female elephant's hunger to remove, the big-trunked male elephant / tender-branched yā tree will strip / full of love, O friend, is the path he went!",
 "translation": "He has great love for you, and he will surely return to bestow his grace. O friend, on the path he has taken, a great-trunked male elephant strips the tender bark of the yā tree to appease the hunger of its female mate. Such is the loving nature of the path he travels.",
 "modern": "தோழியே! அவர் உன் மீது மிகுந்த அன்பு உடையவர்; உனக்கு அருள் செய்யவும் செய்வார். பெண் யானையின் பசியைப் போக்குவதற்காக, பெரிய துதிக்கையையுடைய ஆண் யானையானது மெல்லிய கிளைகளையுடைய யா மரத்தின் பட்டையை உரித்து ஊட்டும். அத்தகைய அன்புடைய காட்சிகளைக் கொண்ட வழியில்தான் அவர் சென்றுள்ளார்.",
 "explanation": "The friend (தோழி) is speaking to the heroine (தலைவி) to comfort her during the hero's absence in the harsh desert (பாலை) landscape. She assures the heroine that the hero is full of love and will return soon. To ease her anxiety, the friend describes the path he is traveling, where a large-trunked male elephant strips the bark of a tender-branched yā tree to feed its hungry female mate. This image of tender care in a dry desert serves as an implied metaphor (uḷḷuṟai uvamam), suggesting that the hero, witnessing such love in nature, will be reminded of his own love and hasten back. Key words include 'நசை' (desire/love), 'பிடி' (female elephant), 'வேழம்' (male elephant), and 'யாஅம்' (yā tree).",
